I have everything needed to trace the full POST /api/owners path. Here is the complete picture.

## Overview: the request flow

`POST /api/owners` is served by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)`. There is no explicit `@PostMapping` in the controller class — the mapping comes from the generated `OwnersApi` interface it implements (`@RequestMapping(method=POST, value="/owners")`). The controller class carries `@RequestMapping("/api")`, so the effective path is `/api/owners`. The V2 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) only handles paginated GET listing, not create.

Note: much of the described "create" validation/business logic lives directly in the controller, NOT in the service. The service layer is a thin passthrough to the repository.

---

## 1. The controller method (the POST /api/owners handler)

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class declaration and constructor (lines 67-91):
```java
@RestController
@CrossOrigin(exposedHeaders = "errors, content-type")
@RequestMapping("/api")
public class OwnerRestControllerV1 implements OwnersApi {

    /** Dedicated audit logger; emits one line per successful owner create. */
    private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");

    private final ClinicService clinicService;
    private final OwnerMapper ownerMapper;
    private final PetMapper petMapper;
    private final VisitMapper visitMapper;

    public OwnerRestControllerV1(ClinicService clinicService,
                                 OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
                                 PetMapper petMapper,
                                 VisitMapper visitMapper) {
        this.clinicService = clinicService;
        this.ownerMapper = ownerMapper;
        this.petMapper = petMapper;
        this.visitMapper = visitMapper;
    }
```

The `addOwner` handler (lines 118-262). This is the entire create method, executed top-to-bottom — every validation and side-effect in order:
```java
    @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
    @Override
    public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
        // Normalize the address up front so every downstream use (the required-field check,
        // household-duplicate detection, the shared household id and the stored/returned value)
        // works from the same canonical form.
        String normalizedAddress = normalizeAddress(ownerFieldsDto.getAddress());
        List<String> missingFields = new ArrayList<>();
        if (isBlank(ownerFieldsDto.getFirstName())) {
            missingFields.add("firstName");
        }
        if (isBlank(ownerFieldsDto.getLastName())) {
            missingFields.add("lastName");
        }
        // Reject an address that is blank once normalized (e.g. whitespace-only input).
        if (isBlank(normalizedAddress)) {
            missingFields.add("address");
        }
        if (isBlank(ownerFieldsDto.getCity())) {
            missingFields.add("city");
        }
        if (isBlank(ownerFieldsDto.getTelephone())) {
            missingFields.add("telephone");
        }
        if (!missingFields.isEmpty()) {
            throw new InvalidOwnerFieldsException(missingFields);
        }
        // A supplied registration date may not lie in the future ...
        if (ownerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate() != null
            && ownerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate().isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {
            throw new FutureRegistrationDateException(ownerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate());
        }
        // Determine the effective registration date ...
        LocalDate effectiveRegistrationDate = ownerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate() != null
            ? ownerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate()
            : LocalDate.now();
        effectiveRegistrationDate = toBusinessDay(effectiveRegistrationDate);
        // Reject the request once the day's owner-creation limit is reached ...
        int ownersRegisteredToday = countOwnersRegisteredOn(effectiveRegistrationDate);
        if (ownersRegisteredToday >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY) {
            throw new DailyOwnerLimitExceededException(effectiveRegistrationDate);
        }
        // Flag a bulk signup once more than 80 owners have already been created for this day.
        boolean bulkSignupWarning = ownersRegisteredToday > BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD;
        // Reject the request when the owner's city is already full (>= 50 owners).
        if (countOwnersInCity(ownerFieldsDto.getCity()) >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY) {
            throw new CityAtCapacityException(ownerFieldsDto.getCity());
        }
        // Postcode is optional; when present must be a 4-digit value valid for the city.
        validatePostcode(ownerFieldsDto.getCity(), ownerFieldsDto.getPostcode());
        // Normalize the telephone into E.164 form; invalid -> 400.
        String normalizedTelephone = toE164(ownerFieldsDto.getTelephone());
        // Email is optional; when present must be valid and is stored lower-cased.
        String normalizedEmail = normalizeEmail(ownerFieldsDto.getEmail());
        // Derive the household id up front ...
        String normalizedLastName = collapse(ownerFieldsDto.getLastName());
        String householdId = householdId(normalizedLastName, ownerFieldsDto.getPostcode());
        boolean sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
        // Consolidated identity-key duplicate detection ...
        String identityKey = identityKey(normalizedTelephone, normalizedEmail, householdId);
        boolean identityInUse = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
            .anyMatch(existing -> identityKey.equals(
                identityKey(existing.getTelephone(), existing.getEmail(), existing.getHouseholdId())));
        if (identityInUse) {
            throw new DuplicateOwnerIdentityException(identityKey);
        }
        // Household duplicate block (bypassed by sharesHousehold) ...
        boolean householdMemberExists = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
            .anyMatch(existing -> householdId.equals(existing.getHouseholdId()));
        if (householdMemberExists && !sharesHousehold) {
            throw new DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException(ownerFieldsDto.getLastName(), normalizedAddress);
        }
        HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
        Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
        owner.setAddress(normalizedAddress);
        owner.setTelephone(normalizedTelephone);
        owner.setEmail(normalizedEmail);
        owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
        owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
        owner.setHouseholdSize(countHouseholdMembers(householdId) + 1);
        owner.setBulkSignupWarning(bulkSignupWarning);
        owner.setRegistrationDate(effectiveRegistrationDate);
        owner.setCustomerCode(customerCode(
            deriveRegion(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity()), normalizedTelephone, owner.getLastName()));
        // Soft-match (possible duplicate) detection ...
        Owner possibleDuplicateOwner = sharesHousehold ? null : findPossibleDuplicate(
            owner.getLastName(), owner.getPostcode(), normalizedTelephone);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(possibleDuplicateOwner != null);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(possibleDuplicateOwner == null ? null : possibleDuplicateOwner.getId());
        this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
        OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        // AUDIT side-effect: emit an audit-trail line for the successful create.
        AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), ownerDto.getMembershipLevel());
        headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
            .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
        return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
    }
```
(I trimmed some inline comments above for brevity; the verbatim comments are in the file lines 118-262. The private helper methods invoked — `normalizeAddress`, `toBusinessDay`, `countOwnersRegisteredOn`, `countOwnersInCity`, `validatePostcode`, `toE164`, `normalizeEmail`, `collapse`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `countNamesakes`, `countHouseholdMembers`, `customerCode`, `deriveRegion`, `findPossibleDuplicate`, `hash8` — and the constants `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY=50`, `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY=100`, `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD=80`, `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS`, etc. are all defined in the same file, lines 358-730.)

Key custom validation helpers worth noting verbatim (all throw `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` → HTTP 400):
- `toE164(String)` lines 659-692 — strips separators, forces `+` + 8-15 digits, enforces national-number length (`+61`→9, `+1`→10).
- `normalizeEmail(String)` lines 716-730 — regex `^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$`, rejects disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), lower-cases.
- `validatePostcode(String,String)` lines 623-639 — optional; 4 digits; region range check.

---

## 2. The generated API interface (source of the POST mapping and `@Valid`)

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java` (generated by OpenAPI Generator)

The `@Validated`-annotated interface (line 44) declares the actual HTTP mapping and body validation (lines 52, 79-87):
```java
    String PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners";
    ...
    @RequestMapping(
        method = RequestMethod.POST,
        value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,
        produces = { "application/json" },
        consumes = { "application/json" }
    )
    default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
        @Parameter(name = "OwnerFieldsDto", description = "The pet owner", required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
    ) {
        ...
    }
```
The `@Valid @RequestBody` here is what triggers Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` (item 4) before the controller override runs.

---

## 3. The service-layer method(s)

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`

The create path calls `saveOwner` (lines 232-237) and, during its validation loops, `findAllOwners` (lines 126-129). Both are transactional passthroughs — no business logic, no security annotations:
```java
    @Override
    @Transactional
    public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
        ownerRepository.save(owner);

    }
```
```java
    @Override
    @Transactional(readOnly = true)
    public Collection<Owner> findAllOwners() throws DataAccessException {
        return ownerRepository.findAll();
    }
```
The interface is `ClinicService` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java`). No `@PreAuthorize`/authorization on the service.

---

## 4. The Owner entity — all Bean Validation annotations

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (lines 35-86 hold the fields/annotations)
```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "owners")
public class Owner extends Person {
    @Column(name = "address")
    @NotEmpty
    private String address;

    @Column(name = "city")
    @NotEmpty
    private String city;

    @Column(name = "telephone")
    @NotEmpty
    @Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$",
